#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Àmbit"

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:12
msgid ""
"This is a static review of the assigned reference-data directory "
"`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives`: 1,438 files totaling 78,066,788 "
"bytes. The inventory is complete; semantic reading was stratified across "
"the principal formats and legal families within the 24,000-token sample "
"cap. I reviewed the BOE consolidated IVA text and its extraction "
"sidecars, a regional tax article and sidecars, a 2026 BOE derogation "
"resolution, two dated XML amendment records, the 2026 Modelo 390 "
"extraction, and the complete bundled PDF provenance note. I also parsed "
"metadata in all 443 extracted JSON sidecars and checked each declared "
"source digest against its on-disk source. This is not a review of current"
" law, an exhaustive reading of every norm, or a run of the application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:14
msgid ""
"The directory split is 1,326 HTML-directory files (73,526,460 bytes), 16 "
"PDF-directory files (3,556,937 bytes), and 96 XML records (983,391 "
"bytes). By format there are 442 HTML source pages, 443 extracted JSON "
"sidecars, 444 Markdown files, 96 XML files, four PDFs, and nine plain-"
"text form transcriptions. The additional Markdown files are corpus "
"provenance and the PDF extraction sidecar. The HTML source pages have "
"matching JSON/Markdown extractions; filenames identify 271 article-"
"specific excerpts, nine additional provisions named as `da` excerpts, and"
" 162 broader document pages. Those counts describe naming/layout, not "
"legal completeness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:16
msgid "Product capability and knowledge represented"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:18
msgid ""
"The corpus supplies documentary reference material across Spanish "
"national tax law, tax administration procedure, regulations, bilateral "
"tax conventions, regional tax provisions and prescribed form layouts. Its"
" filenames are weighted toward ministerial orders, statutes, royal "
"decrees and BOE references: 518 names begin `orden`, 491 `ley`, 163 `rd`,"
" 130 `boe`, 63 `convenio`, 23 `real`, 13 `rdl`, and 12 `rdleg`. "
"Representative full texts include the IVA Law 37/1992, IRPF Law 35/2006, "
"Corporate Tax Law 27/2014, General Tax Law 58/2003, and the IVA and IRPF "
"implementing regulations (Royal Decrees 1624/1992 and 439/2007). Article-"
"level files make selected provisions individually addressable. The sample"
" includes VAT exemptions and exports, the personal minimum in IRPF, and "
"corporate-tax rules on taxable base and related-party transactions. These"
" are source statements, not executed formulas or legal conclusions (Ley "
"37/1992, art. 20 "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/html/ley-37-1992-art-20.html.extracted.md`),"
" Ley 37/1992, art. 21 "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/html/ley-37-1992-art-21.html.extracted.md`),"
" Ley 35/2006, art. 57 "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/html/ley-35-2006-art-57.html.extracted.md`),"
" Ley 27/2014, arts. 10 and 18 "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/html/ley-27-2014-art-10.html.extracted.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:20
msgid ""
"The inventory also covers regional differences and treaty text. For "
"example, the Andalucía article excerpt states region-specific "
"personal/family minimum amounts and points back to the common IRPF "
"statute; its extracted Markdown is one of several small, article-scoped "
"records. This supports a potential workflow that needs a region or "
"provision-specific reference, but no consumer code is in this chunk, so "
"the user's actual ability to select region, tax year, or treaty is "
"unverified (Andalucía Law 5/2021, art. 23 bis "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/html/andalucia-"
"ley-5-2021-art-23-bis.html.extracted.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:22
msgid ""
"HTML originals from BOE preserve publication-page context and navigation,"
" while the parallel `.extracted.json` and `.extracted.md` files provide "
"normalized text units. The JSON records contain schema version, "
"`source_kind`, status, source path and SHA-256, preprocessor "
"name/version, attribution, and the extracted units. All 443 JSON sidecars"
" parsed; all report status `ok`, every source path resolves, and every "
"recorded digest matches the referenced file. The 442 HTML extractions "
"identify `normatives-html` version 1.4; the single PDF extraction "
"identifies `corpus-pdf` version 1.2. The unit counts vary from 1 for a "
"short article to 479 in the sampled consolidated Royal Decree 1175/1990 "
"extraction. These checks establish local extraction-to-source "
"consistency, not the source's legal authority, completeness, or "
"freshness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:24
msgid ""
"The XML branch preserves date-stamped provision/version records rather "
"than only one consolidated view. The sampled December 2025 XML record "
"contains Article 17 of RDL 16/2025 and a provision amending Corporate Tax"
" rules with effects for tax periods beginning in 2025; a separate record "
"identifies a June 2026 version of a model 296 logical-layout annex. A "
"sampled consolidated IVA BOE page identifies itself as informational and "
"says its latest published update is 28 February 2026. Together, these "
"examples show version and publication dates matter: the directory does "
"not have one uniform effective date, and correct downstream selection "
"would need to reconcile document, provision, tax year and effective date."
" No such selector is visible in this data-only chunk (dated RDL 16/2025 "
"Article 17 "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/xml/rdl-16-2025-art-17.xml`), dated"
" 2026 model 296 amendment "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/xml/boe-a-2008-18497-ai-3-redaction-20260624.xml`),"
" consolidated IVA source page "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/html/ley-37-1992.html`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:26
msgid "Forms and provenance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:28
msgid ""
"The PDF area is a mixed set of four publisher-served PDF captures, nine "
"transcriptions of form text, one provenance record, and the 2026 Modelo "
"390 extraction pair. The captures include the 2003 Modelo 185 annex, two "
"Modelo 721 layouts (2023 and an amendment in 2024), and the BOE's January"
" 2026 order updating Modelo 390 and several IVA reporting models. Its "
"extracted text explains the changes to models 303, 322, 353 and 390 and "
"the electronic VAT books; the extraction is paged text from a legal "
"instrument, not a complete interactive filing service or a declaration "
"calculator (Modelo 390 source and extraction "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/pdf/boe-a-2026-1761-modelo-390-form.pdf.extracted.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:30
msgid ""
"`pdf/PROVENANCE.md` distinguishes the four captures from nine manually "
"typed annex transcriptions. It documents that the transcriptions were "
"produced from scans or PDFs and that seven are ASCII-folded while two "
"retain accents; this variation is deliberate and can affect exact-caption"
" citations. The note says formula declarations cite these transcriptions "
"for `required_text` checks, a relationship that synthesis should verify "
"against the formula and source-catalogue code. It also records that the "
"source image for the Modelo 296 transcription was withdrawn and cannot "
"now be checked at the cited address; this is a statement in the bundled "
"provenance record, not an external liveness check. It describes the 2003 "
"Modelo 185 PDF as a genuine capture despite failing the project's later "
"BOE-identifier classifier, and says that classifier's remit excludes "
"these source files. These notes provide useful provenance qualifications "
"but do not independently verify each transcription (provenance record, "
"captures (`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/pdf/PROVENANCE.md`), "
"transcription method and formula-caption role "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/pdf/PROVENANCE.md`), withdrawn "
"Modelo 296 image "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/pdf/PROVENANCE.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:32
msgid ""
"One local metadata inconsistency is confirmed: the 2026 Modelo 390 PDF's "
"extraction JSON says attribution is unavailable because no acquisition-"
"manifest entry matched, while the neighboring provenance record lists the"
" same file as a BOE capture, its retrieval date, and the official BOE PDF"
" address. This may reflect separate provenance systems, but the JSON "
"alone loses source attribution; no consumer impact is established (PDF "
"extraction metadata "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/pdf/boe-a-2026-1761-modelo-390-form.pdf.extracted.json`),"
" provenance entry "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/normatives/pdf/PROVENANCE.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:34
msgid "Security, quality and follow-up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:36
msgid ""
"The reviewed content is public legal and administrative reference "
"material; I found no customer records or credentials in the samples. The "
"files themselves contain static HTML, extracted text, XML, PDFs and "
"provenance notes. Nothing in this chunk executes filing, changes user "
"data, makes network calls, or enforces authorization. Raw HTML is "
"publisher markup, so any application behavior that renders it needs a "
"separate rendering/sanitization review; this data inspection does not "
"establish that it is rendered. Likewise, inaccurate or stale reference "
"material could affect downstream advice or calculations only if and how "
"the application consumes it. The key trust boundary is therefore the "
"provenance, temporal selection and interpretation of bundled text, not an"
" access-control mechanism implemented here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:38
msgid ""
"A specific context-loss risk is visible in the representation: the raw "
"Ley 37/1992 BOE page carries the explicit warning that its consolidated "
"text is informational and has no legal value, plus its update date. The "
"extracted Markdown begins at provision text and does not retain that "
"page-level notice or date. JSON retains the file hash and attribution, "
"but not an explicit legal-as-of field. If a downstream consumer indexes "
"only the extraction, it must recover legal status and effective date "
"elsewhere; whether it does so is unresolved. Similarly, source hashes "
"prove that sidecars match the bundled bytes, not that the bundled bytes "
"match an official publication or the law applicable to a user's period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/197-normative-reference-corpus.md:40
msgid ""
"The strong local qualities are broad primary-source coverage, article-"
"level organization, typed extraction metadata, pinned hashes, and "
"explicit provenance for hard-to-read form annexes. The main unresolved "
"quality questions are coverage completeness by tax/topic/year, source "
"freshness, effective-date resolution, reconciliation of extractions with "
"the raw publisher page, and validation of manual form transcriptions. No "
"tests or runtime behavior are supplied by this chunk. Synthesis should "
"trace which modules consume `.html`, `.extracted.json`, `.extracted.md`, "
"`.xml` and transcription assets; whether they preserve source attribution"
" and “informational” caveats; how they select redactions and tax periods;"
" and how `required_text` citations are verified."
msgstr ""

